<code>assert this.size() > 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.peek().compareTo(this.get(i)) <= 0;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.size() > 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.peek().compareTo(this.get(i)) <= 0;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.size() == 0 || \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), this.get(i)) <= 0;</code>

Explanation:
- The assert statement checks if the queue is not empty (`this.size() != 0`).
- If the queue is not empty, it ensures that the element returned by `peek()` is less than or equal to every other element in the queue.
- The comparison is done using the `comparator()` method, which returns the comparator used by the priority queue.
- The `\forall` quantifier is used to ensure that the condition holds for all elements in the queue.
